@endpoint("/authn-api/mfa/{id}", "get", #{`operationId`:"getStep",`tags`:#["Sign-in"],`summary`:"What a second-factor or emailed-factor step's page shows",`description`:"The step's view for the page `page` names (`totp`, `webauthn`, `backup-code`, `password`, `setup`, `email-code`, `email-link`, `email-link-open`, `post-login`; the step's own where left out), as facts and no words: the person, the ways round the factor asked for, the set-up step's choice and its authenticator app's `otpauth:` URI, the passkey ceremony's description, an emailed factor's state — and `csrf`. Refused (400) where the page could never be drawn for the step: an expired step, a code page for somebody with no authenticator app, a passkey page for somebody holding no passkey (any key may answer the step since #1135; the authentication policy decides whether this use is open). `key` names the passkey a person chose where the passkey policy offers them one by one.\n\nThe door of the sign-in surface's `GET /authn/totp, /authn/webauthn, /authn/backup-code, /authn/password-factor, /authn/mfa-setup, /authn/email-code, /authn/email-link, /authn/email-link/open, /authn/post-login`.",`parameters`:#[#{`name`:"id",`in`:"path",`required`:true,`description`:"The second-factor or emailed-factor step's id: a bearer capability, as the `mfa` its page was opened with.",`schema`:null}],`responses`:#{`200`:#{`description`:"The answer.",`content`:#{`application/json`:#{`schema`:null}}},`400`:#{`description`:"Refused: `{ ok: false, errors }` — the body, the id, or the act itself.",`content`:#{`application/json`:#{`schema`:null}}},`default`:#{`description`:"A refusal or a failure.",`content`:#{`application/json`:#{`schema`:null}}}},`security`:#[],`x-mirrors`:"GET /authn/totp, /authn/webauthn, /authn/backup-code, /authn/password-factor, /authn/mfa-setup, /authn/email-code, /authn/email-link, /authn/email-link/open, /authn/post-login"})
